docbook-to-man.ts: "name \- text" on the manual pages' NAME lines.

The DocBook-to-man transform separates a page's names from its purpose
with \(em. The NAME line of a manual page is "name \- text" by the -man
convention, which whatis and man -k read: catman and the whatis tools
take the text after " - " as the description. The separator is now \-.
Only that line of every page changes.

--- a/programs/dtdocbook/tpt/docbook-to-man.ts	2026-11-20 12:03:13
+++ b/programs/dtdocbook/tpt/docbook-to-man.ts	2026-11-20 12:03:13
@@ -98,7 +98,7 @@
 -
 #
 GI:		REFPURPOSE
-StartText:	\s\\(em\s
+StartText:	\s\\-\s
 EndText:	^
 -
 #
